{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1560339-psiad-teleporters","id":1560339,"title":"Psiad teleporters","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: \u00c6on"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-06-04T06:09:58-07:00","id":1560339,"title":"Psiad teleporters","content":"So, for the people here, how would you run psiad teleporters? Since, RAW, teleportation can't be a primary aptitude for them, meaning even with maxed-out Psi and edges you can only get a single teleportation mode to 4. I understand this is partially because, lore-wise, psiads grow into their powers, naturally moving from Psi 1 to 2, and you need 3 to do teleportation, and I guess partially because teleportation + quantakinesis might be unbalanced (not sure about that one)?<br /> <br /> However, say you do want to allow psiads to have teleportation as a primary aptitude, say because you're running a sci-fi psiad-only game. If so, how would you approach this? I can see a few methods myself:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Just make teleportation available as a primary mode, you just can't put dots into it until you reach Psi 3. Feels like the easiest solution, but also like it might cause some balance issues, making the pressure to reach Psi 3 far bigger than it already is.</li> <li>An edge that allows for starting at Psi 3 (**** Strong Potential), meaning you can just pick teleportation as your primary. Xp cost for the edge would be the same as a dot of Psi, so I think it <i>should</i> be balanced? Of course, that's not dealing with possible balance considerations of being able to access both teleportation and QK.</li> <li>Same as before, but the edge is instead (** Complex Psionics) and it makes Teleportation and QK your only primary aptitudes. Should resolve any balance issues from having both advanced aptitudes as primaries, but I'm uncertain of how big of a deal those are. Might be too much of a nerf.</li> <li>Instead of making QK the default higher aptitude, allow for choosing between Teleportation and QK. A fairly easy one mechanically, but it sort of breaks Aeon's lore. Fine if you're not using that, and instead adapting the system for a different universe though.</li> <li>On that note, if using a setting or time period where QK is not available (Aberrant), just allow for picking any aptitude as a third primary when hitting Psi 3. Would have the benefit of making psiads a bit more useful in Aberrant too, given that they're already underpowered as is.</li> </ol>Any feedback or opinions on this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28973-kenod","name":"kenod","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-04T11:54:01-07:00","id":1560352,"title":"","content":"Technically, point 2 isn't choosing it as a main - you'd still only get to assign your three dots to your actual Aptitudes, build up to Psi 3, and then get Teleportation so that you can push one of its modes higher than usual.<br /> <br /> Within the main setting, QK and Teleportation are big deals. Another setting might have different precepts; commonly, people with psi might not have BK and VK but might have teleportation, or the setting might have no conception of QK, since that's a very, very Trinity Continuum conceit that other settings might just break up and divy between other manifestations of psychic powers, if at all; anything in Fundamentals involving Corruption in particular is likely to get tossed out altogether instead of adapted, since that deals with the Aberrants' major issues which is a pretty much a defining facet of how TC handles powers.<br /> <br /> The Aeon Aexpansion also had a section on using psions in place of psiads for handling other scifi story styles. You might want to look there; it has guidelines for modifying things to make them more like The Tomorrow People, Scanners, or the X-Men (assuming you're not using Aberrant to run that one).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-04T17:09:34-07:00","id":1560356,"title":"","content":"Cue &quot;The Rancher and the Farmer Should be Friends&quot; and picture groups of Psiads, Psions, Novas, and Talents trying to function as a team.<br /> <br /> Now, we need a new category. Not a Mesmerist, a Psiad, or a Psion. We need a <b>Psychic! </b>start them as you would Psiads and once you've maxed out one of your powers You've got the option to pick a second base pair and <b>Quantakinesis</b> and <b>Teleportation </b>could be and optional pair. I'd have some extra requirement for the pair.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 06-04-2026, 08:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}